1
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:24,860
Catching the winds of the passing seasons,
shining, the ultimate harem.

2
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:37,460
lightly leaping over these hectic times,
diving into the town, playing at being a hero.

3
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:39,420
I wanna, time is a paradise

4
00:00:39,420 --> 00:00:45,080
Only the quick ones,
so that we pick them up.

5
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:49,160
Because your bare face
suits you best.

6
00:00:49,740 --> 00:00:50,840
Let it rain

7
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:55,020
Everybody can do, we've started running

8
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:58,240
Dreams never stop, you know

9
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:02,460
Let's go, no regrets tomorrow too

10
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:03,400
Let it run

11
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:07,680
Everybody can do, just a little

12
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:15,040
It doesn't hurt,
holding on to a rowdy curiosity

13
00:01:15,870 --> 00:01:18,040
We flew strong and high

14
00:01:29,590 --> 00:01:31,580
Soba shop rebuilding plan

15
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:42,880
It's cold.
Can we have some hot soba or something?

16
00:01:43,180 --> 00:01:43,860
Sounds good.

17
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:49,820
It used to be a shop that never got any customers,
you know.

18
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:53,160
Hey, hey.

19
00:01:54,820 --> 00:01:56,440
Looks like we might be able to get in soon.

20
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:00,900
Hey, you bastard, that's dangerous!

21
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:03,260
Bastard.

22
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:04,320
Senpai.

23
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:10,159
This guy,

24
00:02:10,209 --> 00:02:16,920
You're the gourmet critic who's been all over TV and magazines lately,
Cho-Goro.

25
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:20,760
This flavor is no ordinary taste.

26
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:24,520
As always,
this shop front is no ordinary one.

27
00:02:24,570 --> 00:02:25,780
Is the proprietor here?

28
00:02:26,060 --> 00:02:27,480
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes.

29
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:30,700
It's you, Sensei. Please, come inside.

30
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:34,040
Hey, that's cutting in line, you bastard.

31
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:35,500
Now, now, senpai.

32
00:02:36,620 --> 00:02:37,460
Yes, right this way.

33
00:02:39,420 --> 00:02:40,600
Such efficient handling!

34
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:49,340
Acting so high and mighty, we've been
waiting out in the cold for three hours!

35
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:17,480
This soba is no ordinary soba.

36
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:18,300
Thank you very much.

37
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:18,780
Thank you very much.

38
00:03:19,980 --> 00:03:23,100
Here comes Professor Omaeda's
"no ordinary" line!

39
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:26,220
As expected, the soba here is top-quality.

40
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:28,360
Ordinary or not, I don't care what it is.

41
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:30,800
Once you've finished eating,
hurry up and vacate your seat.

42
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:34,220
Owner, my acquaintances too -

43
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:36,740
I want them to savor
this extraordinary soba.

44
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:39,440
Can you arrange about 200 servings?

45
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:43,940
Two hundred servings would
come to over 100,000 yen.

46
00:03:43,940 --> 00:03:47,180
Owner, I am Japan's
number one gourmet critic.

47
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:49,380
I am Chōgorō!

48
00:03:49,380 --> 00:03:52,080
Of course, I won't need payment.

49
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:54,080
Please, enjoy it with everyone.

50
00:03:57,420 --> 00:03:59,400
Keep up the good work from now on.

51
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:00,120
Thank you very much.

52
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:04,120
So they're finally gone.

53
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:06,540
Well, now it's our turn.

54
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:08,420
What?

55
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:10,220
Hey, old man.

56
00:04:10,220 --> 00:04:11,780
What do you mean, you're closing?

57
00:04:11,780 --> 00:04:14,320
We came here with one wish:
to eat some hot soba.

58
00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:17,040
We've been waiting three
hours in this freezing cold!

59
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:21,940
The critic took all the
soba with him... eh...

60
00:04:21,940 --> 00:04:28,760
It's us who want to cry! We never
should have let this magazine feature us.

61
00:04:29,140 --> 00:04:29,660
Well, come on.

62
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:40,860
I see, so customers suddenly increased because it was featured in this magazine.
They're all crowding in and gobbling it up

63
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:42,600
What an outrageous guy.

64
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:47,940
Damn it, if it's come to this,
I don't care if it's a little bad.

65
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:50,800
Isn't there a shop that serves hot soba?

66
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:54,080
Senpai, how about this soba shop?

67
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:54,920
What?

68
00:04:56,660 --> 00:04:57,400
Pardon me.

69
00:05:01,540 --> 00:05:04,640
There's no sign whatsoever
that any customers have come in!

70
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:06,880
This place is dangerous. Let's get out.

71
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:08,200
Why?

72
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:11,800
Don't you get it? It's not normal
for a place to be this unpopular.

73
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:16,320
They're bound to serve soba so awful that
one bite and you'll never want to eat it again.

74
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:22,840
Are you customers?

75
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:25,080
That was the plan, but...

76
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:26,000
Thank you very much.

77
00:05:27,060 --> 00:05:28,200
What's wrong?

78
00:05:28,640 --> 00:05:31,380
Actually, you two are our fifth customers.

79
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:35,100
The fifth customers today? Well, I guess
that's about right, judging by how things look.

80
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:37,580
No, no,
you're our fifth customers since we opened.

81
00:05:37,580 --> 00:05:37,920
What?

82
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:39,900
Wait, wait, hold on.

83
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,740
When did you open this shop?

84
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:42,900
Three years ago.

85
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:44,100
Three years ago?

86
00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:47,800
I'll have it made right away.

87
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:48,760
What'll it be?

88
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:52,200
Well, actually,
my stomach suddenly started acting up.

89
00:05:54,460 --> 00:05:56,300
Senpai, that's pitiful.

90
00:05:56,300 --> 00:05:57,780
Let's at least eat some for him.

91
00:05:57,780 --> 00:06:01,440
What if we eat soba here and
our stomachs really do go bad?

92
00:06:01,840 --> 00:06:05,740
If anything happens, the Nakagawa
Zaibatsu medical team will take care of it.

93
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:11,280
Let's be the fifth customer for him.

94
00:06:11,660 --> 00:06:12,020
Please.

95
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:14,460
Fine, fine, I get it.

96
00:06:14,460 --> 00:06:16,820
I'll be the fifth victim, then.

97
00:06:24,820 --> 00:06:26,140
Sorry to keep you waiting.

98
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:28,960
This soba looks awful.

99
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:31,260
Let's eat quickly and
get back to the station.

100
00:06:35,960 --> 00:06:37,200
Don't stare at me.

101
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:38,600
S-sorry.

102
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:40,940
You're worried about what the customers think,
aren't you?

103
00:06:40,940 --> 00:06:41,980
Y-yes.

104
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:44,400
I'll tell you my opinion
after I finish eating.

105
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:47,160
So until I'm done eating,
go away over there.

106
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:47,780
Yes.

107
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:54,460
Just plain soba, nothing special.

108
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:56,880
It's not so bad that it's inedible, but

109
00:07:00,820 --> 00:07:01,420
W-wait, this is

110
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:03,140
What's wrong, Nakagawa?

111
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:05,500
Sir, I'd like to ask you something.

112
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:07,060
Yes, what is it?

113
00:07:07,660 --> 00:07:08,600
Could this soba

114
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:11,460
be made with buckwheat
flour from Yamada Farm?

115
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:20,860
Yamada Farm is the farm of Yamada Denroku, the
buckwheat flour master known only to those in the know.

116
00:07:23,940 --> 00:07:33,460
The buckwheat flour produced there is said to be the best in Japan,
but it's hard to get, and even in the Nakagawa Group's

117
00:07:33,460 --> 00:07:39,640
cooking division, only a few shops use it. I've been close with Little Yamada for years,
so we get it cheap for home.

118
00:07:39,640 --> 00:07:43,940
Just as I thought.
The soy sauce used in the dashi

119
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:47,900
is made by Sato Brewery, isn't it? Yes.

120
00:07:48,580 --> 00:07:52,220
Sato Brewery, which has been making
handmade soy sauce since its founding,

121
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:56,340
carries on the traditional flavors of Kyushu,
said to be the birthplace of soy sauce.

122
00:07:56,880 --> 00:08:01,020
The soy sauce made here is truly
called the soy sauce of soy sauces.

123
00:08:01,660 --> 00:08:04,980
No, it's not just the soy sauce.
The bonito flakes and kelp too,

124
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:08,760
producing this rich dashi
is definitely top-grade.

125
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:12,800
And the green onions are wonderfully firm and glossy.
Such excellent ingredients.

126
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:14,580
And the shichimi chili pepper,

127
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,900
its seven flavors create
an exquisite harmony.

128
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:19,940
The spiciness is also just right.

129
00:08:20,340 --> 00:08:23,320
They must be using very
carefully selected ingredients.

130
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:26,320
Hey, hey,
why would they use such amazing ingredients

131
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:28,260
to make nothing but ordinary soba like this?

132
00:08:28,260 --> 00:08:29,640
Ordinary, you say?

133
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:32,140
Senpai, look at your own bowl.

134
00:08:33,220 --> 00:08:34,160
Before you knew it?

135
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:37,200
That's just how truly delicious food is.

136
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:40,240
It goes naturally into your body.

137
00:08:41,900 --> 00:08:44,380
Old man, a refill! Another bowl, please!

138
00:08:44,380 --> 00:08:44,840
Yes.

139
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:51,020
It really is quite good
when you savor it slowly.

140
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:52,220
Right?

141
00:08:52,220 --> 00:08:55,480
With flavor like this,
you should advertise more.

142
00:08:55,860 --> 00:08:58,000
I'm really not good at flashy things.

143
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,640
Even so, it's strange.

144
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:03,440
With taste like this, you'd expect
customers to come through word of mouth.

145
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:07,000
There's a deep reason why no customers come.

146
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,000
A deep reason?

147
00:09:08,300 --> 00:09:10,120
I'll never forget it. Three years ago.

148
00:09:11,780 --> 00:09:15,820
On a day when light snow was falling,
this shop opened.

149
00:09:19,780 --> 00:09:23,120
I was nervous,
waiting for the first customer to arrive.

150
00:09:23,120 --> 00:09:24,060
And then...

151
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:27,220
Sorry.

152
00:09:27,220 --> 00:09:28,400
Eeeeehh?

153
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:37,580
What, it was you? Did the famous Ōmaeda-sensei come all this way just to eat?
No, he came to use the toilet.

154
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:38,620
Aaaaaah.

155
00:09:40,820 --> 00:09:46,660
So this was a soba shop. It was so
ordinary I didn't notice. Perfect timing.

156
00:09:46,660 --> 00:09:56,260
Then let's eat here. I'll make it right away.
Since you were our first customer, I put my heart into it.

157
00:09:57,220 --> 00:09:57,720
Here you go.

158
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:23,240
How was it?

159
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:24,640
This chef is no ordinary man.

160
00:10:24,640 --> 00:10:26,220
It's nothing special, this taste.

161
00:10:31,580 --> 00:10:33,700
That'll be 700 yen.

162
00:10:35,780 --> 00:10:40,360
Surely you don't have
no idea who I am, do you?

163
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:44,020
I'm the gourmet critic Ōmaeda Chōgorō.

164
00:10:45,140 --> 00:10:48,480
Yes, so one bowl of kakesoba is 700 yen.

165
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:53,140
I'm Japan's number one gourmet critic,
Ōmaeda Chōgorō, you know!

166
00:10:53,140 --> 00:10:56,220
Yes, so a bowl of kakesoba is 700 yen.

167
00:10:58,220 --> 00:10:59,660
I'm talking to you!

168
00:10:59,820 --> 00:11:02,480
So, if it's 700 yen,

169
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:05,220
That's why I'm telling you, it's on you!

170
00:11:05,340 --> 00:11:06,780
since it's 700 yen,

171
00:11:06,780 --> 00:11:10,560
Well, unfortunately I make
it a rule not to carry cash.

172
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:12,720
Could you accept this instead?

173
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:16,780
It's pure gold, so it should be
worth twenty or thirty thousand.

174
00:11:16,780 --> 00:11:18,700
Th-thank you very much.

175
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:23,220
Owner, what's the name of this shop?

176
00:11:23,300 --> 00:11:25,280
Y-yes, it's Soba Tanaka.

177
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:27,260
Soba Tanaka.

178
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:30,140
I'll remember that.

179
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:38,040
In the end, that fountain pen
turned out to be a total fake.

180
00:11:38,040 --> 00:11:39,480
That's a petty story.

181
00:11:39,480 --> 00:11:41,760
What surprised me was one week later.

182
00:11:41,760 --> 00:11:45,180
They absolutely trashed my shop in it.

183
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:49,100
It's not fit for human consumption.

184
00:11:49,100 --> 00:11:51,780
Even if the world forgives it,
I won't forgive it.

185
00:11:51,780 --> 00:11:53,360
Minus seven stars.

186
00:11:53,360 --> 00:11:54,700
That's awful.

187
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:56,420
Don't you dare display it!

188
00:11:56,420 --> 00:11:59,600
But since our shop was featured after all,

189
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:01,840
it's only going to give us a negative image,
you know.

190
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:04,080
Still, what a terrible article.

191
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:06,740
It's all completely off-base criticism.

192
00:12:06,740 --> 00:12:08,680
Is it spite because he
couldn't eat for free?

193
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:12,480
Even taking away the soba I was
supposed to eat is unforgivable.

194
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:15,300
Giving soba this good a bad
review could sink the shop!

195
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:19,580
For someone who can't even tell good
taste to call himself a food critic.

196
00:12:19,580 --> 00:12:21,080
It's a ridiculous story.

197
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:24,720
Right, I'll make him learn
what happens when he angers me.

198
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:25,740
Hey, proprietor.

199
00:12:25,740 --> 00:12:27,940
Yes, if it's something I can do.

200
00:12:27,940 --> 00:12:30,380
Leave it to me. I have a good idea.

201
00:12:30,380 --> 00:12:32,140
You'd better wash your neck and wait for me.

202
00:12:32,140 --> 00:12:33,580
It's you, Chōgorō!

203
00:12:39,420 --> 00:12:41,580
To make Omaeda eat his words,

204
00:12:41,580 --> 00:12:43,400
a certain amount of sacrifice is necessary.

205
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:45,040
You're prepared for that, I hope?

206
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:46,060
Y-yes.

207
00:12:46,060 --> 00:12:46,980
Then, from here on,

208
00:12:46,980 --> 00:12:50,560
we begin the operation to make
Omaeda Chōgorō eat his words.

209
00:12:57,840 --> 00:12:58,960
What are you planning?

210
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:02,400
To impress the old-school critics,
an ordinary shop like this just won't do.

211
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:04,380
It needs tradition and prestige.

212
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:05,440
I see.

213
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:09,440
So the idea is to give it the look of a
place that has weathered years of rumors.

214
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:10,760
Exactly.

215
00:13:21,220 --> 00:13:23,520
These ordinary bowls won't do!

216
00:13:26,980 --> 00:13:28,860
My shop...

217
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:32,540
Senpai, is there anything I can help with?

218
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:33,895
Anything will do.

219
00:13:33,945 --> 00:13:37,040
Have them bring something that
conveys tradition and dignity!

220
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,140
Understood!

221
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:41,460
Next up...

222
00:13:48,380 --> 00:13:50,660
Ryo-san, what are you doing?

223
00:13:50,660 --> 00:13:52,120
You're just in time.

224
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:54,800
Didn't you two make

225
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:56,520
bowls in art class at school?

226
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:58,880
Yeah, but they're covered in dust,

227
00:13:58,880 --> 00:13:59,880
and they have cracks too.

228
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:01,420
Even better, then.

229
00:14:01,420 --> 00:14:02,600
Go bring them.

230
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:04,300
Borrow one for your friend too.

231
00:14:04,300 --> 00:14:05,460
Got it, Ryo-san.

232
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:12,980
You're awake

233
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,140
We borrowed these from
museums around the world.

234
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:40,840
They're all pieces that tell
the story of human history.

235
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:41,980
There, there.

236
00:14:42,512 --> 00:14:46,240
I feel it's unnatural for an ordinary
soba shop to have things like this.

237
00:14:46,240 --> 00:14:48,940
It's fine, it's better to put
on a bit of a show like this.

238
00:14:48,940 --> 00:14:52,400
That's right, let's say this one
is an opening gift from Cleopatra.

239
00:14:56,440 --> 00:14:57,840
That's absurd.

240
00:14:58,300 --> 00:14:59,360
I think that's about enough.

241
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:01,100
Here we go.

242
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:04,100
While we're at it,
why don't we break one of the pillars too?

243
00:15:04,520 --> 00:15:08,400
Please stop! If you cut that,
the whole building will collapse.

244
00:15:08,400 --> 00:15:09,640
Good point.

245
00:15:16,100 --> 00:15:17,800
Good, good, excellent work.

246
00:15:17,800 --> 00:15:20,080
With this, the shop is all set.

247
00:15:20,980 --> 00:15:21,760
Now just the

248
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:23,860
N-no way

249
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:26,940
Please stop, not that,
anything but that, please stop

250
00:15:26,940 --> 00:15:29,940
What the critics respond to is an eccentric shop owner,
you see.

251
00:15:29,940 --> 00:15:32,120
Don't go that far, stop!

252
00:15:32,120 --> 00:15:33,320
Don't use that creepy voice.

253
00:15:38,340 --> 00:15:39,940
Hey, that bicycle is

254
00:15:42,620 --> 00:15:44,300
You're slacking off again, Kankichi!

255
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:45,260
Yo!

256
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:46,720
Nakagawa!

257
00:15:47,060 --> 00:15:48,940
I'm done. Come on, get over here.

258
00:15:49,180 --> 00:15:50,080
B-but...

259
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:51,740
What are you embarrassed about?

260
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:53,220
Just as I thought, you're slacking off!

261
00:15:53,520 --> 00:15:55,200
I'm telling Chief Ohara!

262
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:56,040
Hey, you!

263
00:15:56,340 --> 00:15:56,600
Hey!

264
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:10,960
Retirement...

265
00:16:11,460 --> 00:16:12,620
Me, of all people...

266
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:17,480
I see, you're that happy about it?

267
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:19,880
He's lamenting his own misfortune, you know.

268
00:16:20,340 --> 00:16:21,680
Now the stage is set.

269
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:24,000
Nakagawa, arrange the cherry blossoms.

270
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:24,400
Yes.

271
00:16:24,840 --> 00:16:27,000
All that's left is to corner our prey.

272
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:39,180
Is there really a delicious soba
shop around here with a line forming?

273
00:16:39,180 --> 00:16:41,671
Yes, according to information from viewers,

274
00:16:41,721 --> 00:16:44,580
a line two kilometers
long forms there every day.

275
00:16:44,860 --> 00:16:46,200
Isn't that it?

276
00:16:50,740 --> 00:16:52,102
Wow, that's amazing.

277
00:16:52,152 --> 00:16:55,380
Is this entire line
leading to the soba shop?

